course: dictionary
lesson: 8722
title: Separate: apart, or to divide
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Separate has two jobs. As an adjective, it means not joined together, or different. «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots.» The nuts are in lots of different places, not in one pile.
explain: As a verb, separate means to move things apart, or to divide a mixture into its parts. In science, a sieve separates big bits from small ones. Ask yourself: are things being kept apart, or are they being pulled apart?
explain: Separate can also mean to stop living together. «When parents are splitting up, they are separating or divorcing, and a child can feel ill from the worry.» This is a hard meaning, and it is never the child's fault.
fact: As an adjective, separate is said SEP-rut, as in two separate rooms.
fact: As a verb, separate is said SEP-a-rate, as in separate the eggs.
fact: Useful phrases include «keep separate», «separate into», «go their separate ways» and «separate from».
fact: «Keep raw meat separate from other food» means keep them apart so germs do not spread.
fact: «Writing was invented separately in Mesopotamia», so the word separately means in different places, on its own.
exercise: «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots.» What does separate mean here? | Round and smooth | *Apart, in different places | Very quickly | Joined together in one heap
exercise: «Keep raw meat separate from other food.» What does separate mean here? | Washed under the tap | *Kept apart, not mixed together | Cooked for a long time | Put in the fridge with the other food
exercise: «A sieve separates big bits from small ones.» What does separates mean? | Washes away | Joins together | Melts | *Divides into different parts
test: How do you say separate as an adjective? | *SEP-rut | SEP-ret | sep-AR-ate | SEP-a-rate
test: «Writing was invented separately in Mesopotamia.» What does separately mean? | Together in one place | *In different places, on its own | Quickly | Written down again later
exam: «In 1337, England and Scotland were separate rival kingdoms.» What does separate mean in this sentence? | *Apart and different, not joined as one | Joined together under one king | Very small in size | Sent away by post
